  (text "FROM THE HAND-WRITTEN NETLIST THIS SHEET REPLACES (verbatim; the part notes are on each part's Note field):\n\nAUTHORITATIVE for connectivity. The ASCII drawing in mod-channels.md is a REPRESENTATION of this file.\n\nTHE DRAWING SHOWS ONE CHANNEL OF FOUR and says so. This file writes all four out, because four identical\nchannels sharing one reference buffer is exactly the shape where \"identical\" hides a defect: three channels\nwired one way and the fourth not is invisible in a drawing of one.\n\nTHE SHARED REFERENCE IS THE SAFETY ARGUMENT. V_ref comes from DAC channel 7, so a CLR zeroes it along with the\nsignal channels and every jack parks at 0 V. A fixed divider in its place would leave the offset standing and\npin all four jacks at -10 V indefinitely, with no MISO to notice. That is why DAC_CH7 is a port here and not a\nlocal net.\n\n--- the shared offset reference -----------------------------------\n\nR-OPAMP-IN AND R-BIAS-DAC ARE NOT DRAWN ON THIS PAGE UNDER THEIR NAMES. The drawing spells the series\nresistors `[1k]`, which no checker can bind to a refdes, and R-BIAS-DAC appears on no drawing at all - its row\nsays \"at every DAC output pin\" and there are six populated channels. Both are netted here, which is the first\ntime either is in a file a tool reads.\n\n--- the op-amps: five halves in three OPA2197 packages ----------------\n\nU-MOD-A holds the shared reference buffer (A) and channel 1 (B); U-MOD-B channels 2 (A) and 3 (B); U-MOD-C\nchannel 4 (A) and one of the module's two spare halves (B), tied off as a follower on the star. Supply pins\nare netted, with one C-DECOUPLE at each.\n\n--- mod channel 1, from DAC ch2 -----------------------------------\n\n--- mod channel 2, from DAC ch3 -----------------------------------\n\n--- mod channel 3, from DAC ch4 -----------------------------------\n\n--- mod channel 4, from DAC ch5 -----------------------------------\n\n[VREF_MOD] V_ref, buffered once and shared by all four channels. The one node whose error appears as a common\nshift rather than as four channels disagreeing.\n\n[SPARE_C_OUT] The spare half's follower loop." (at 40.64 147.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid 16348580-b7f1-5902-9e0a-1694c6f21a12))
  (text "THIS CIRCUIT IS ON BOTH MODULE BOARDS (ADR 0023). Page main holds its main-board parts, page jack the parts behind the panel; the labels here join the two pages, and on the boards J-B2B-MOD joins them. Each board places its own page." (at 60.96 30.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid b6ad9a2a-2352-5f68-99e1-f6d9f3d99efb))
